INTERVIEW NOTES
============================================================

1.  These are beginner-friendly / normal coding approaches.
2.  Nested loops are easy to understand but may take O(n^2) time.
3.  Set and Map can improve many lookup and frequency problems.
4.  Two Sum with nested loops takes O(n^2); a Map solution can take O(n)
    average time.
5.  Longest substring with nested loops is an easy approach; sliding
    window is the optimized interview approach.
6.  Three Sum uses sorting and two pointers to avoid duplicate triplets.
7.  Object.hasOwn(obj, key) checks whether a property belongs directly
    to the object.
